1.bug_scenario:
The user mounted a Select component with an empty dataSource but passed both defaultValue and fillProps:  

  ReactDOM.render(<Select fillProps="name" defaultValue="jack" ></Select>, mountNode);

They expected the input to display “jack” (as shown in the reference image), but nothing is rendered.  The presence of fillProps triggers code paths that override the normal label logic and don’t fall back to the raw defaultValue when the dataSource is empty.
